IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bkv-law`

-- The grounds for refusing access in the Informationsfreiheitsgesetz (IFG) §§ 3 to 6, spelled out as rules: § 3 nos. 1 to 8, § 4(1), § 5(1) and § 6, with the parts of § 5(2) and (3) that settle the weighing.
-- bkv-law.l4 asks them as one fact, `another ground for refusing access applies`, and encodes § 3 no. 4 only as far as it turns on BKV § 9(5) or another statutory duty.
-- This module adds rules beside it and changes nothing in it: the seat layer bkv-ifg-seat.l4 computes `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` here and passes it in as that field.
-- Each ground reads facts the requester can state and characterisations that stay inputs because they are judgments; the trailing comment on each field says which (F or J) and why. NOTES.md, forks F6 to F13, gives the readings.
-- The three modalities of the text are flattened into one yes/no per ground: 'besteht nicht' (§ 3, § 6 sentence 1), 'soll abgelehnt werden' (§ 4(1)), 'darf nur gewährt werden, soweit' (§ 5(1), § 6 sentence 2). Where the text says 'soll' or 'in der Regel' an input carries the atypical case.
-- Law layer. Target compiler: main.
-- Every quotation is a verbatim slice of a deposited source in ../../registers/source-bundle/, checked with srcrefs.py.
-- German is the only authoritative language; English names are glosses.

§ `Facts about the information requested, one record for each ground`

-- One record per ground, so that a rule names only the facts it reads. Every field is a BOOLEAN about the information requested or the request.
-- F: a fact a person can state. J: a judgment or a legal characterisation, kept as an input and never guessed (ENCODING-GUIDE section 4).
-- 'Disclosure' is the English gloss for 'das Bekanntwerden der Information' (§ 3) and 'die vorzeitige Bekanntgabe' (§ 4(1)).

-- IFG § 3 no. 1, limbs a to g. Limb g has three alternatives, written as three fields.
DECLARE `Facts about section 3 no. 1` HAS
    `disclosure could adversely affect international relations` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast: 'nachteilige Auswirkungen haben kann'
    `disclosure could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Bundeswehr` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast
    `disclosure could adversely affect interests of internal or external security` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast
    `disclosure could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast
    `disclosure could adversely affect matters of external financial control` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast
    `disclosure could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast
    `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast
    `disclosure could adversely affect the claim of a person to a fair trial` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast
    `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast

-- IFG § 3 no. 2.
DECLARE `Facts about section 3 no. 2` HAS
    `disclosure could endanger public safety` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast: 'gefährden kann'

-- IFG § 3 no. 3, limbs a and b: 'wenn und solange'.
DECLARE `Facts about section 3 no. 3` HAS
    `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast: 'beeinträchtigt werden'; the 'wenn und solange' is read as of the day of the decision
    `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of the deliberations of an authority` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast: 'beeinträchtigt werden'; BVerwG 7 C 4.11 para. 31 reads 'notwendige Vertraulichkeit' into it too

-- IFG § 3 no. 4, the limbs other than 'durch Rechtsvorschrift': the general administrative rule on classified information, a professional secret, a special official secret. bkv-law.l4 has the limb 'durch Rechtsvorschrift'.
DECLARE `Facts about section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` HAS
    `the information is subject to a duty of secrecy set by the general administrative rule on classified information` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F, that the document is so classified; whether the classification is itself lawful is not in the deposited text
    `the information is subject to a professional secret` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a legal notion borrowed from other law
    `the information is subject to a special official secret` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a legal notion borrowed from other law

-- IFG § 3 no. 5: all three together.
DECLARE `Facts about section 3 no. 5` HAS
    `the information comes from another public body` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F
    `the information was drawn in only temporarily` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F
    `the information is not meant to become part of the own records of the authority` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, the intention of the authority

-- IFG § 3 no. 6.
DECLARE `Facts about section 3 no. 6` HAS
    `disclosure is apt to impair fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast: 'geeignet wäre'
    `disclosure is apt to impair economic interests of the social insurance funds` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast: 'geeignet wäre'

-- IFG § 3 no. 7: both together.
DECLARE `Facts about section 3 no. 7` HAS
    `the information was collected or transmitted in confidence` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F, how the information was received
    `the interest of the third party in confidential treatment still persists at the time of the request` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, an interest of the third party 'im Zeitpunkt des Antrags'

-- IFG § 3 no. 8: the claim does not exist against these bodies.
DECLARE `Facts about section 3 no. 8` HAS
    `the authority asked is an intelligence service` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F, which authority was asked
    `the authority asked performs tasks within section 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act and the information concerns them` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, borrowed from the Security Clearance Act, § 10 no. 3, which is not deposited

-- IFG § 4(1): the first five fields are sentences 1 and 2, the last is the 'soll'.
DECLARE `Facts about section 4(1)` HAS
    `the information is a draft of a decision` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F
    `the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, 'unmittelbare Vorbereitung' is a legal characterisation
    `the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F
    `a paper of that kind nevertheless serves the immediate preparation of a decision` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, the 'regelmäßig' of sentence 2 displaced by an atypical case
    `premature disclosure would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a forecast: 'vereitelt würde'; 'soweit und solange'
    `the case is atypical, so that the application should not be refused` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, the 'soll' of sentence 1 displaced by an atypical case

-- IFG § 5(1) to (3). The weighing of § 5(1) sentence 1 is the field `the interest of the requester ... outweighs ...`; § 5(2) and (3) settle it in two cases.
DECLARE `Facts about section 5` HAS
    `the information contains personal data of a third party` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F, with a data-protection term borrowed (not deposited)
    `the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation is not deposited
    `the third party has consented to access` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F
    `the consent of the third party was express` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F
    `the interest of the requester in the information outweighs the interest of the third party in excluding access` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, the balancing; § 5(2) and (3) settle it in two cases (rules below)
    `the personal data come from documents about the service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F
    `the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a legal notion borrowed from other law
    `the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F
    `the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F
    `the case is atypical, so that section 5(3) does not settle the weighing` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, the 'in der Regel' of § 5(3) displaced by an atypical case

-- IFG § 6, sentences 1 and 2.
DECLARE `Facts about section 6` HAS
    `the information contains intellectual property` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a legal characterisation of the material
    `the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access requested` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, 'entgegensteht'
    `the information contains a trade or business secret` IS A BOOLEAN  -- J, a legal notion not defined in the deposited text
    `the person concerned has consented to access to the trade or business secret` IS A BOOLEAN  -- F

-- All the facts about one request, one record for each ground.
DECLARE `Facts bearing on the grounds for refusing access` HAS
    `facts for section 3 no. 1` IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 1`
    `facts for section 3 no. 2` IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 2`
    `facts for section 3 no. 3` IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 3`
    `facts for section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty`
    `facts for section 3 no. 5` IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 5`
    `facts for section 3 no. 6` IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 6`
    `facts for section 3 no. 7` IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 7`
    `facts for section 3 no. 8` IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 8`
    `facts for section 4(1)` IS A `Facts about section 4(1)`
    `facts for section 5` IS A `Facts about section 5`
    `facts for section 6` IS A `Facts about section 6`

-- The grounds, for the list of those that apply. `section 3 no. 4 by a statute` is the limb that bkv-law.l4 encodes (BKV § 9(5) and another statutory duty).
DECLARE `Ground for refusing access` IS ONE OF
    `section 3 no. 1`
    `section 3 no. 2`
    `section 3 no. 3`
    `section 3 no. 4 by a statute`
    `section 3 no. 4 by classification or by a professional or official secret`
    `section 3 no. 5`
    `section 3 no. 6`
    `section 3 no. 7`
    `section 3 no. 8`
    `section 4(1)`
    `section 5(1)`
    `section 6`

§ `IFG § 3 no. 1: harm to a protected public interest`

-- No. 1 is a list of interests: if disclosure could adversely affect any of them the claim does not exist. 'kann' is a forecast, so each limb is a judgment the person supplies.
-- src:ifg-3:2 | Der Anspruch auf Informationszugang besteht nicht,
-- src:ifg-3:3 | 1. wenn das Bekanntwerden der Information nachteilige Auswirkungen haben kann auf
-- src:ifg-3:4 | a) internationale Beziehungen,
-- src:ifg-3:5 | b) militärische und sonstige sicherheitsempfindliche Belange der Bundeswehr,
-- src:ifg-3:6 | c) Belange der inneren oder äußeren Sicherheit,
-- src:ifg-3:7 | d) Kontroll- oder Aufsichtsaufgaben der Finanz-, Wettbewerbs- und Regulierungsbehörden,
-- src:ifg-3:8 | e) Angelegenheiten der externen Finanzkontrolle,
-- src:ifg-3:9 | f) Maßnahmen zum Schutz vor unerlaubtem Außenwirtschaftsverkehr,
-- src:ifg-3:10 | g) die Durchführung eines laufenden Gerichtsverfahrens, den Anspruch einer Person auf ein faires Verfahren oder die Durchführung strafrechtlicher, ordnungswidrigkeitsrechtlicher oder disziplinarischer Ermittlungen,
@ref IFG § 3 no. 1, limbs a to g (src:ifg-3:2-10)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 1`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 no. 1 IFG bars access` MEANS
        facts's `disclosure could adversely affect international relations`
    OR facts's `disclosure could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Bundeswehr`
    OR facts's `disclosure could adversely affect interests of internal or external security`
    OR facts's `disclosure could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities`
    OR facts's `disclosure could adversely affect matters of external financial control`
    OR facts's `disclosure could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade`
    OR facts's `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case`
    OR facts's `disclosure could adversely affect the claim of a person to a fair trial`
    OR facts's `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations`

§ `IFG § 3 no. 2: public safety`

-- src:ifg-3:11 | 2. wenn das Bekanntwerden der Information die öffentliche Sicherheit gefährden kann,
@ref IFG § 3 no. 2 (src:ifg-3:11)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 2`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 no. 2 IFG bars access` MEANS
        facts's `disclosure could endanger public safety`

§ `IFG § 3 no. 3: international negotiations and the deliberations of authorities`

-- 'wenn und solange': the claim is out of the way only while the impairment lasts. BVerwG 7 C 4.11 para. 31 says access is 'grundsätzlich nur aufgeschoben' and that the necessary confidentiality of § 3 no. 3 a is also to be read into limb b.
-- The inputs are therefore answered as of the day of the decision, and a 'false' later is a different question; the encoding does not model the later day.
-- src:ifg-3:12 | 3. wenn und solange
-- src:ifg-3:13 | a) die notwendige Vertraulichkeit internationaler Verhandlungen oder
-- src:ifg-3:14 | b) die Beratungen von Behörden beeinträchtigt werden,
-- src:bverwg-7c4-11-excerpt:7 | b) § 3 Nr. 3 Buchst. b IFG steht dem Informationsanspruch ebenso wenig entgegen. Nach dieser Bestimmung besteht der Anspruch auf Informationszugang nicht, wenn und solange die Beratungen von Behörden beeinträchtigt werden. Angesichts des Schutzzwecks der Vorschrift ist die allein in § 3 Nr. 3 Buchst. a IFG erwähnte „notwendige Vertraulichkeit“ auch auf die behördlichen Beratungen zu beziehen. Mit der Formulierung „solange“ macht das Gesetz deutlich, dass der Informationszugang grundsätzlich nur aufgeschoben ist. Die Dauer dieses Aufschubs bestimmt sich danach, ob der Schutz der Vertraulichkeit weiterhin eine Offenlegung der Beratungsinterna verbietet. Der Abschluss des laufenden Verfahrens bildet dabei keine unüberwindbare zeitliche Grenze (vgl. Beschluss vom 18. Juli 2011 - BVerwG 7 B 14.11 - NVwZ 2011, 1072 Rn. 5).
@ref IFG § 3 no. 3, limbs a and b (src:ifg-3:12-14), as BVerwG 7 C 4.11 para. 31 reads it (src:bverwg-7c4-11-excerpt:7)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 3`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 no. 3 IFG bars access` MEANS
        facts's `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations`
    OR facts's `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of the deliberations of an authority`

§ `IFG § 3 no. 4: the limbs other than a statutory provision`

-- bkv-law.l4 has `section 3 no. 4 IFG bars access under the reading`: a duty 'durch Rechtsvorschrift', BKV § 9(5) or another. The other limbs of no. 4 are here: a duty set by the general administrative rule on classified information,
-- or a professional secret, or a special official secret. They are asked as facts or legal characterisations, since the texts that define them are not deposited.
-- src:ifg-3:15 | 4. wenn die Information einer durch Rechtsvorschrift oder durch die Allgemeine Verwaltungsvorschrift zum materiellen und organisatorischen Schutz von Verschlusssachen geregelten Geheimhaltungs- oder Vertraulichkeitspflicht oder einem Berufs- oder besonderen Amtsgeheimnis unterliegt,
@ref IFG § 3 no. 4, the limbs other than 'durch Rechtsvorschrift' (src:ifg-3:15)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 no. 4 IFG bars access for a reason other than a statutory duty` MEANS
        facts's `the information is subject to a duty of secrecy set by the general administrative rule on classified information`
    OR facts's `the information is subject to a professional secret`
    OR facts's `the information is subject to a special official secret`

§ `IFG § 3 no. 5: information drawn in only temporarily`

-- All three: information of another public body, drawn in only temporarily, which is not to become part of the authority's own records.
-- src:ifg-3:16 | 5. hinsichtlich vorübergehend beigezogener Information einer anderen öffentlichen Stelle, die nicht Bestandteil der eigenen Vorgänge werden soll,
@ref IFG § 3 no. 5 (src:ifg-3:16)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 5`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 no. 5 IFG bars access` MEANS
        facts's `the information comes from another public body`
    AND facts's `the information was drawn in only temporarily`
    AND facts's `the information is not meant to become part of the own records of the authority`

§ `IFG § 3 no. 6: fiscal and economic interests`

-- src:ifg-3:17 | 6. wenn das Bekanntwerden der Information geeignet wäre, fiskalische Interessen des Bundes im Wirtschaftsverkehr oder wirtschaftliche Interessen der Sozialversicherungen zu beeinträchtigen,
@ref IFG § 3 no. 6 (src:ifg-3:17)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 no. 6 IFG bars access` MEANS
        facts's `disclosure is apt to impair fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce`
    OR facts's `disclosure is apt to impair economic interests of the social insurance funds`

§ `IFG § 3 no. 7: information received in confidence`

-- Both: the information was received in confidence AND the third party's interest in confidential treatment persists at the time of the request ('im Zeitpunkt des Antrags').
-- The article's footnote 8 assumes the statement was submitted as non-confidential: that is the first field being false.
-- src:ifg-3:18 | 7. bei vertraulich erhobener oder übermittelter Information, soweit das Interesse des Dritten an einer vertraulichen Behandlung im Zeitpunkt des Antrags auf Informationszugang noch fortbesteht,
@ref IFG § 3 no. 7 (src:ifg-3:18)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 7`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 no. 7 IFG bars access` MEANS
        facts's `the information was collected or transmitted in confidence`
    AND facts's `the interest of the third party in confidential treatment still persists at the time of the request`

§ `IFG § 3 no. 8: intelligence services and security-sensitive bodies`

-- The claim does not exist against the intelligence services, and against other federal bodies as far as they perform tasks within § 10 no. 3 of the Sicherheitsüberprüfungsgesetz, which is not deposited.
-- src:ifg-3:19 | 8. gegenüber den Nachrichtendiensten sowie den Behörden und sonstigen öffentlichen Stellen des Bundes, soweit sie Aufgaben im Sinne des § 10 Nr. 3 des Sicherheitsüberprüfungsgesetzes wahrnehmen.
@ref IFG § 3 no. 8 (src:ifg-3:19)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 3 no. 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 no. 8 IFG bars access` MEANS
        facts's `the authority asked is an intelligence service`
    OR facts's `the authority asked performs tasks within section 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act and the information concerns them`

§ `IFG § 4(1): drafts and the immediate preparation of a decision`

-- Sentence 2 matters for a statement an outside body sent in: 'Nicht der unmittelbaren Entscheidungsvorbereitung nach Satz 1 dienen regelmäßig ... Gutachten oder Stellungnahmen Dritter.'
-- 'regelmäßig' is a presumption: such a paper is taken not to prepare the decision unless the person says the case is atypical (the field `a paper of that kind nevertheless serves ...`).
-- src:ifg-4:2 | (1) Der Antrag auf Informationszugang soll abgelehnt werden für Entwürfe zu Entscheidungen sowie Arbeiten und Beschlüsse zu ihrer unmittelbaren Vorbereitung, soweit und solange durch die vorzeitige Bekanntgabe der Informationen der Erfolg der Entscheidung oder bevorstehender behördlicher Maßnahmen vereitelt würde. Nicht der unmittelbaren Entscheidungsvorbereitung nach Satz 1 dienen regelmäßig Ergebnisse der Beweiserhebung und Gutachten oder Stellungnahmen Dritter.
@ref IFG § 4(1) sentences 1 and 2 (src:ifg-4:2)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 4(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the information serves the immediate preparation of a decision under section 4(1) IFG` MEANS
    IF facts's `the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party`
    THEN facts's `a paper of that kind nevertheless serves the immediate preparation of a decision`
    ELSE (facts's `the information is a draft of a decision`
          OR facts's `the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision`)

-- 'soll abgelehnt werden': in the usual case the application is refused; the field `the case is atypical ...` is the exception.
-- 'soweit und solange': the forecast of frustration is asked as of the day of the decision.
@ref IFG § 4(1) sentence 1 (src:ifg-4:2)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 4(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 4(1) IFG says the application should be refused` MEANS
        `the information serves the immediate preparation of a decision under section 4(1) IFG` facts
    AND facts's `premature disclosure would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures`
    AND NOT (facts's `the case is atypical, so that the application should not be refused`)

§ `IFG § 5(1): personal data of a third party`

-- The weighing of § 5(1) sentence 1 is a judgment, the input `the interest of the requester ... outweighs ...`.
-- Two paragraphs settle it: § 5(2) says it 'überwiegt nicht' for data from documents about the third party's service or office relationship or a mandate, and for data under a professional or official secret (read as two cases, each enough);
-- § 5(3) says it outweighs 'in der Regel' when the data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number and the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way.
-- The categorical § 5(2) is taken to prevail over the 'in der Regel' of § 5(3) when both apply (fork F10). § 5(4), the names of case handlers, is not encoded (NOTES.md).
-- src:ifg-5:3 | (2) Das Informationsinteresse des Antragstellers überwiegt nicht bei Informationen aus Unterlagen, soweit sie mit dem Dienst- oder Amtsverhältnis oder einem Mandat des Dritten in Zusammenhang stehen und bei Informationen, die einem Berufs- oder Amtsgeheimnis unterliegen.
-- src:ifg-5:4 | (3) Das Informationsinteresse des Antragstellers überwiegt das schutzwürdige Interesse des Dritten am Ausschluss des Informationszugangs in der Regel dann, wenn sich die Angabe auf Name, Titel, akademischen Grad, Berufs- und Funktionsbezeichnung, Büroanschrift und -telekommunikationsnummer beschränkt und der Dritte als Gutachter, Sachverständiger oder in vergleichbarer Weise eine Stellungnahme in einem Verfahren abgegeben hat.
@ref IFG § 5(2) and (3) (src:ifg-5:3-4)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 5`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the interest in access outweighs the interest of the third party under section 5 IFG` MEANS
        NOT (facts's `the personal data come from documents about the service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party` OR facts's `the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret`)
    AND ((facts's `the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number` AND facts's `the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way` AND NOT (facts's `the case is atypical, so that section 5(3) does not settle the weighing`))
         OR facts's `the interest of the requester in the information outweighs the interest of the third party in excluding access`)

-- Sentence 1: access to personal data only as far as the weighing favours it or the third party consented.
-- Sentence 2: for the special categories of Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation, which is not deposited, only if the third party consented expressly, whatever the weighing.
-- src:ifg-5:2 | (1) Zugang zu personenbezogenen Daten darf nur gewährt werden, soweit das Informationsinteresse des Antragstellers das schutzwürdige Interesse des Dritten am Ausschluss des Informationszugangs überwiegt oder der Dritte eingewilligt hat. Besondere Kategorien personenbezogener Daten im Sinne des Artikels 9 Absatz 1 der Verordnung (EU) 2016/679 des Europäischen Parlaments und des Rates vom 27. April 2016 zum Schutz natürlicher Personen bei der Verarbeitung personenbezogener Daten, zum freien Datenverkehr und zur Aufhebung der Richtlinie 95/46/EG (Datenschutz-Grundverordnung) (ABl. L 119 vom 4.5.2016, S. 1; L 314 vom 22.11.2016, S. 72; L 127 vom 23.5.2018, S. 2) in der jeweils geltenden Fassung dürfen nur übermittelt werden, wenn der Dritte ausdrücklich eingewilligt hat.
@ref IFG § 5(1) (src:ifg-5:2)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 5`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`access to the personal data is allowed under section 5(1) IFG` MEANS
    IF facts's `the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation`
    THEN facts's `the third party has consented to access` AND facts's `the consent of the third party was express`
    ELSE (`the interest in access outweighs the interest of the third party under section 5 IFG` facts OR facts's `the third party has consented to access`)

@ref IFG § 5(1) (src:ifg-5:2)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 5`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 5(1) IFG bars access to personal data` MEANS
        facts's `the information contains personal data of a third party`
    AND NOT (`access to the personal data is allowed under section 5(1) IFG` facts)

§ `IFG § 6: intellectual property and trade or business secrets`

-- Sentence 1: the claim does not exist as far as the protection of intellectual property stands in the way. Sentence 2: trade or business secrets only with the consent of the person concerned.
-- The article's footnote 8 assumes no trade secrets and no copyright-protected material.
-- src:ifg-6:2 | Der Anspruch auf Informationszugang besteht nicht, soweit der Schutz geistigen Eigentums entgegensteht. Zugang zu Betriebs- oder Geschäftsgeheimnissen darf nur gewährt werden, soweit der Betroffene eingewilligt hat.
@ref IFG § 6 sentences 1 and 2 (src:ifg-6:2)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about section 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 6 IFG bars access` MEANS
        (facts's `the information contains intellectual property` AND facts's `the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access requested`)
     OR (facts's `the information contains a trade or business secret` AND NOT (facts's `the person concerned has consented to access to the trade or business secret`))

§ `The grounds composed`

-- A ground for refusal other than § 3 no. 4 in any of its limbs: nos. 1 to 3 and 5 to 8, § 4(1), § 5(1) and § 6. One line for each ground, in the order of the text.
@ref IFG § 3 nos. 1 to 3 and 5 to 8, § 4(1), § 5(1) and § 6, composed
GIVEN grounds IS A `Facts bearing on the grounds for refusing access`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` MEANS
        `section 3 no. 1 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 1`)
    OR `section 3 no. 2 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 2`)
    OR `section 3 no. 3 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 3`)
    OR `section 3 no. 5 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 5`)
    OR `section 3 no. 6 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 6`)
    OR `section 3 no. 7 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 7`)
    OR `section 3 no. 8 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 8`)
    OR `section 4(1) IFG says the application should be refused` (grounds's `facts for section 4(1)`)
    OR `section 5(1) IFG bars access to personal data` (grounds's `facts for section 5`)
    OR `section 6 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 6`)

-- The same, with the limbs of § 3 no. 4 that bkv-law.l4 does not encode. This is what the seat layer passes to bkv-law.l4 as `another ground for refusing access applies`.
-- The limb 'durch Rechtsvorschrift' stays in bkv-law.l4, so a statutory duty is not counted twice.
@ref IFG § 3 nos. 1 to 8, § 4(1), § 5(1) and § 6, other than a statutory duty under § 3 no. 4, composed
GIVEN grounds IS A `Facts bearing on the grounds for refusing access`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` MEANS
        `a ground for refusal other than section 3 no. 4 applies` grounds
    OR `section 3 no. 4 IFG bars access for a reason other than a statutory duty` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty`)

§ `Which grounds apply`

-- The grounds that apply to a request, for the person who is refused and asks why. `section 3 no. 4 by a statute` is bkv-law.l4's rule, which depends on the reading of BKV § 9(5).
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground for refusing access`
      reading IS A `Reading of BKV 9(5)`
      request IS A `Request for a document`
      grounds IS A `Facts bearing on the grounds for refusing access`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ground for refusing access applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `section 3 no. 1` THEN `section 3 no. 1 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 1`)
    WHEN `section 3 no. 2` THEN `section 3 no. 2 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 2`)
    WHEN `section 3 no. 3` THEN `section 3 no. 3 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 3`)
    WHEN `section 3 no. 4 by a statute` THEN `section 3 no. 4 IFG bars access under the reading` reading request
    WHEN `section 3 no. 4 by classification or by a professional or official secret` THEN `section 3 no. 4 IFG bars access for a reason other than a statutory duty` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty`)
    WHEN `section 3 no. 5` THEN `section 3 no. 5 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 5`)
    WHEN `section 3 no. 6` THEN `section 3 no. 6 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 6`)
    WHEN `section 3 no. 7` THEN `section 3 no. 7 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 7`)
    WHEN `section 3 no. 8` THEN `section 3 no. 8 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 3 no. 8`)
    WHEN `section 4(1)` THEN `section 4(1) IFG says the application should be refused` (grounds's `facts for section 4(1)`)
    WHEN `section 5(1)` THEN `section 5(1) IFG bars access to personal data` (grounds's `facts for section 5`)
    WHEN `section 6` THEN `section 6 IFG bars access` (grounds's `facts for section 6`)

`all the grounds for refusing access` MEANS
    LIST `section 3 no. 1`,
         `section 3 no. 2`,
         `section 3 no. 3`,
         `section 3 no. 4 by a statute`,
         `section 3 no. 4 by classification or by a professional or official secret`,
         `section 3 no. 5`,
         `section 3 no. 6`,
         `section 3 no. 7`,
         `section 3 no. 8`,
         `section 4(1)`,
         `section 5(1)`,
         `section 6`

GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of BKV 9(5)`
      request IS A `Request for a document`
      grounds IS A `Facts bearing on the grounds for refusing access`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Ground for refusing access`
`the grounds for refusing access that apply` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN ground YIELD `the ground for refusing access applies` ground reading request grounds) `all the grounds for refusing access`
